  "worked_solution": "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+5)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & =1(x+5)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1+1 & =1(-1+5)+B \\\\ 0 & =4+B \\\\ B & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
